|> Exercise
    handle=_construct_dimensionless_output_

    Can one construct a function of signature 
    $$[\s] \ra [1]$$
    given a function $f : [\s] \ra [\s]$?

    !! Given a differentiable function $f: [\s] \ra [\s]$
    !! can one construct a function of signature $[\s] \ra [1]$?

    |> Solution

        Yes: the functions $f'$, $f/f$ (which is $1$ whenever $f \ne 0$,
        else undefined), $\cos \circ f'$,
        and others, all work—another exotic option is

        $$
        f^0
        $$

        which is identically $1$ on $\dom f$, that 
        works becase
        !! outputs the
        !! requisite dimensionless units of $[1]$ because

        $$
        f^n : [\s] \ra [\s^n]
        $$

        more generally for all integers $n$. (And $[\s^0] = [1]$,
        if one can make the latter an article of faith.)

